    <h2>What Does “Cut Out Background from a Photo” Mean?</h2>

    <p>
        Cutting out a background means removing everything behind the main subject of an image. The subject remains intact,
        while the background is deleted or made transparent.
    </p>

    <p>
        This is commonly used for product images, profile photos, and design elements.
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Isolates the main subject</li>
        <li>Removes unwanted background elements</li>
        <li>Creates transparent or custom backgrounds</li>
        <li>Enhances image flexibility</li>
    </ul>

